<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jayadeva</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jayadeva was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> poet of the 12th century, author of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gita-govinda">Gita Govinda</a>, a celebrated poem on the love of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a> and Radha. Tradition places him at the court of the Sena king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lakshman-sena">Lakshman Sena</a>, though <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a> also claims him through the village of Kenduli. His work shaped Vaishnava devotion and the arts across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jayadeva.jpg" alt="Jayadeva" width="320" height="483" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Prateek Pattanaik · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancient_stone_idol_of_poet_Jayadeba_at_Akhandaleswara_Temple,_Prataparudrapura,_Odisha.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
